# No form autocomplete

Browser and password-manager autofill must stay disabled for every form in this project unless the user explicitly asks to enable it.

## Required defaults

- Use the shared `Form` component (`autoComplete="off"` plus hidden decoy username/password/email fields)
- Use `TextField` / `SelectField` (or the same attributes): `autoComplete="new-password"`, `data-1p-ignore`, `data-lpignore`, `data-bwignore`, `data-form-type="other"`, unlock `readOnly` only on focus
- Prefer opaque `name` / `id` values that do not contain `user`, `id`, `login`, `email`, or `password` (e.g. `yora_acct_code`, `yora_signin_code`)
- Fields Chrome treats as username (User ID / Username) must use `disableUsernameAutofill` (`autoComplete="one-time-code"`) and clear autofill on create/login mount
- Prefer `type="text"` with `inputMode` over `type="email"` / `type="tel"` unless a native type is explicitly required
- Field helpers must enforce these attributes and must not allow callers to turn autofill back on

Never enable autofill for login, user creation, user edit, or other forms unless asked.
